I think it's mostly a personal preference, but I generally go for 
foo-proofing of "keeper" items before general enchantment, unless the 
only scroll of enchantment I've got is blessed, in which case it would 
feel like a waste. It seems like I run into rotting/burning/rusting 
monsters on a fairly regular basis and I don't like having to worry 
about it. As for the trade-off, I think in the case of speed boots the 
speed itself is worth more than a few AC points, so you're already 
"ahead," making the trade-off consideration less important. Not that 
that's an airtight argument, but that's the way I think of it.


